## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heightfield_clip.html
- Summary (EN): HeightField Clip clamps a height layer between optional lower and upper limits. It also outputs masks that show which regions were clipped by each limit.
- Résumé (FR) : HeightField Clip borne une couche de hauteur entre deux limites optionnelles et fournit des masques des zones écrêtées.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: heightfield to clamp", "lower: optional per-pixel scaling of the lower limit", "upper: optional per-pixel scaling of the upper limit", "mask: optional per-pixel mask, scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Mask: how much of the clipped height mixes back with the original height", "Compute Range: fills Lower Limit and Upper Limit with the minimum and maximum of the input height", "Lower Limit and Upper Limit: enable and set each limit; a dropper picks the value in the viewport", "Clamped Values: Replace with Limit Value, or Soft Clip", "Soft Clip Direction: smooth transition outside the range (extending the clip) or inside it (narrowing the clip)", "Soft Clip Range: width of the smoothing transition from the limit to the original values"]

- Caveats: ["The page lists no explicit limitations, performance notes or edge cases", "Soft Clip changes values near the limits as well as the clamped values, so it is not a pure hard clamp", "The internal type name cop heightfield_clip is inferred from the page file name, not stated on the page"]

